      "problem": "$\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{6}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{6}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{6}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{6}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{6}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{6}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\sqrt{6}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
